{title: 230 - All Glory, Laud, and Honor}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #230 • ST. THEODULPH • 7.6.7.6.7.5.7.5}
{lyricist: Theodulph of Orleans}
{composer: Melchior Teschner}
{key: Bb}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 230}
{meta: tune ST. THEODULPH}
{meta: meter 7.6.7.6.7.5.7.5}
{meta: category Jesus Christ - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Bb]All [F/A]glory, [Eb]laud, [F7/C]and [Bb]hon or,
[Bb]To [F7]Thee, [Gm]Redeemer, [Bb]King,
[Bb]To [F/A]whom [Bb]the [Eb]lips [F7/C]of [Bb]children
[Bb]Made [F7]sweet [Gm]hosannas [Bb]ring.
[Bb]Thou art [C/E]the [F]King [Cm]of [Dm]Israel,
[Cm]Thou David’s [F]royal Son,
[F/A]Who [Bb]in the [Eb]Lord’s [Bb]name [F/A]comest,
[Bb/D]The [Eb]King [Bb]and [F]Blessed One.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Bb]The [F/A]company [F7/C]of [Bb]angels
[Bb]are [F7]praising [Eb]thee [F]on [Bb]high,
[Bb]and [F/A]we [Bb]with [Eb]all [F7/C]creation
[Bb]in [F7]chorus [Eb]make [F]reply.
[Bb]The people [F]of [Cm]the [Dm]Hebrews
[Cm]with psalms before [F]thee went;
[F/A]our [Bb]prayer and [Eb]praise [Bb]and [F/A]anthems
[Bb/D]before thee [F]we present.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Bb]To [F/A]thee, [Bb]before [F7/C]thy [Bb]passion,
[Bb]they [F7]sang [Gm]their [Eb]hymns [F]of [Bb]praise;
[Bb]to [F/A]thee, [Bb]now [Eb]high [F7/C]exalted,
[Bb]our [F7]melody [F]we [Bb]raise.
[Bb]Thou didst [C/E]accept [Cm]their [Dm]praises;
[Cm]accept the [F]prayers we bring,
[F/A]who [Bb]in all [Eb]good [Bb]delightest,
[Bb/D]thou [Eb]good [Bb]and [F]gracious [Bb]King.
{end_of_verse}
